[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.75]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,10.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(10.5,0);
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8,10} {\draw (-0.2,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.8,0) rectangle (2.8,4);
\draw (2.8,0) rectangle (4.8,8);
\draw (4.8,0) rectangle (6.8,10);
\draw (6.8,0) rectangle (8.8,6);
\foreach \x/\lbl in {1.8/15, 3.8/25, 5.8/35, 7.8/45} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.15) {$\lbl$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,5) {Frequency};
\node[below] at (4.8,-1.0) {Class centre};
\node at (4.8,11.0) {Weekly study hours};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The frequency histogram shows the weekly study hours of students using class centres $15, 25, 35, 45$. How many students studied for more than $30$ hours (class centres $35$ and $45$)?

